export const CONTENT = {"meta":{"title":"2027 — Your Year of Divine Creativity, Divine Love and Divine Wisdom","book":"Consecration Mastery 101","author":"Gideon Abochie","trial_days":14,"trial_weeks":[1,2],"four_fields":["Self","Family","Business","Nation"],"five_dimensions":["Spiritual","Mental","Physical","Social","Financial"]},"weeks":[{"n":1,"month":"January","title":"The Way in the Wilderness","html":"<h2>Week 1 — The Way in the Wilderness</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> January · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jan 3–9</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.&quot; (Isaiah 43:19, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The new thing is God&#x27;s before it is ours. The community does not invent a vision in January; it looks for the way God is already cutting.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Walk the streets of your own neighbourhood in pairs — or, if you cannot meet in person, map your area together online. Write down three places where people are stuck and one thing already being done about each.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord of the work, fill my hands with skill I did not earn, and let nothing I make be made for applause.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the three observations in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And have severed you from other people, that ye should be mine.&quot; (Leviticus 20:26, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Holiness is received before it is practised. We do not love our way into belonging; we belong, and so we learn to love.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Each household names one person in the community it has been treating as scenery. Greet them by name in the next online gathering (or by a direct message) and ask one real question.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, love through me where my affection has run out.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> one sentence in the Book of the Heart — what changed in you when you saw them.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.&quot; (James 1:5, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year&#x27;s first act of wisdom is admitting we lack it, without shame.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the year&#x27;s single question on the first page of the Book of the Mind: <em>what is God already doing here that we have not noticed?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, I lack wisdom; give it without reproach.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the question, dated.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jan 3 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> three observed needs, one named person, one governing question.</p>"},{"n":2,"month":"January","title":"Filled Before Consulted","html":"<h2>Week 2 — Filled Before Consulted</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> January · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jan 10–16</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he hath filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship&quot; (Exodus 35:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Bezalel was not asked whether he felt ready. Skill was given for a work that would outlast him.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> List the skills already present in the community — not the skills you wish you had. Ask three people in the group chat what they are already good at.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker of all things, let my plan begin where Yours already is.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the list in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Let all your things be done with charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 16:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is the operator, not the ornament. A gift given to be seen is not charity even when the gift is good.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one useful thing this week that nobody will know you did. Do not tell the group what it was.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, give me the measure of Your love for someone hard to love.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> only the date and the words <em>done unseen</em> in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For I know that in me (that is, in my flesh,) dwelleth no good thing: for to will is present with me; but how to perform that which is good I find not&quot; (Romans 7:18, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The will is intact and still insufficient. A vision built on resolve alone will fail by February.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write beside last week&#x27;s question: <em>this cannot be done by deciding harder.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let me lean on You and not on my own understanding.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the sentence in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jan 10 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a skills inventory; an unseen act; a written admission of dependence.</p>"},{"n":3,"month":"January","title":"The Heart Indites","html":"<h2>Week 3 — The Heart Indites</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> January · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jan 17–23</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue is the pen of a ready writer.&quot; (Psalm 45:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The hand executes what the heart has already composed. Before you build, find out what you actually care about.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Each person writes one paragraph beginning <em>the thing I cannot stop caring about is…</em> Read them aloud in pairs, not in the group.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me courage to start small and finish truly.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the paragraph in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.&quot; (James 3:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Rivalry is the enemy of a common vision. Comparison turns gifts into weapons.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name quietly one person whose gift makes you uneasy. Pray for them by name on Wednesday and again on Friday.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of mercy, let my kindness be costly and real.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> <em>rivalry named and refused</em> in the Book of the Heart — no other detail.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.&quot; (Philippians 4:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind is consecrated by what it is trained to notice. This is not positive thinking; it is obedience of attention.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> For one day, note every complaint that passes through your mind and answer each with one true thing.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, renew my mind after Christ, not after the age.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the count in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jan 17 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a caring paragraph; rivalry refused; a discipline of attention begun.</p>"},{"n":4,"month":"January","title":"Whatsoever Ye Do","html":"<h2>Week 4 — Whatsoever Ye Do</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> January · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jan 24–30</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Whether therefore ye eat, or drink, or whatsoever ye do, do all to the glory of God.&quot; (1 Corinthians 10:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> There is no sacred/secular division in the Hand. Making and mercy are one motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose one ordinary weekday task and do it this week as an act of worship, with attention to how it is done.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let the work of my hands serve someone I would not have chosen.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the task and how you did it, in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue; but in deed and in truth.&quot; (1 John 3:18, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Affection that never becomes action is not love that has matured.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Turn one of January&#x27;s observed needs into a single concrete act — a meal, a visit, a repair, a ride — or a phone call, a message or a shared document.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, unite my divided heart to fear Your name.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what was done and for whom, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.&quot; (James 1:22, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The first deception is thinking that hearing counted as doing.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Review the month so far: which of your own words have you not kept? Write them down without explanation.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth, take every thought captive to Your Son.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the list in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jan 24 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> one ordinary task offered; one need met; one broken word owned.</p>"},{"n":5,"month":"January","title":"The Vision Fast","html":"<h2>Week 5 — The Vision Fast</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> January · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jan 31 – Feb 6</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it?&quot; (Luke 14:28, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Counting the cost is an act of faith, not of fear.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Estimate honestly what the community can give in 2027 — hours, money, skills — and what it cannot.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, make my work honest when no one is watching.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the estimate in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he said unto his disciples, Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat; neither for the body, what ye shall put on.&quot; (Luke 12:22, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> A fast is not a technique to obtain a vision; it is the admission that we are not fed by our own plans.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> A twenty-four-hour fast from one ordinary comfort, with the time normally spent on it given to prayer for the community.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me see the person I have been treating as scenery.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> one line — what you learned about your dependence — in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he said unto them, Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while.&quot; (Mark 6:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Rest is commanded, not earned. A vision made by exhausted people will be a smaller vision than God intends.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Keep the evening free. No meeting, no planning.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me hear before I answer.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the word <em>rested</em> and the date in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jan 31 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Jan 31):</strong> the three Vision Books are opened. The Three-Faculty Audit is signed by each household. Nothing is launched. the month&#x27;s single question remains pinned at the head of the shared document: <em>what is God already doing here that we have not noticed?</em>*</p>"},{"n":6,"month":"February","title":"Filled for Workmanship","html":"<h2>Week 6 — Filled for Workmanship</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> February · <strong>Dates:</strong> Feb 7–13</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And in cutting of stones, to set them, and in carving of timber, to work in all manner of workmanship.&quot; (Exodus 31:5, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Spirit&#x27;s filling is practical. God cares about the quality of the work, not only the sincerity of the worker.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Identify one thing in your home, your neighbourhood or your online space that is badly made or badly kept, and improve it properly.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the wilderness, cut a road where I can see none.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> before/after note in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And when the LORD saw that Leah was hated, he opened her womb: but Rachel was barren.&quot; (Genesis 29:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> God sees the person who is overlooked. A community&#x27;s vision is judged by who it notices.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Contact someone who has not been spoken to in a month — by visit, call or message. Stay twice as long as feels comfortable.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make my hospitality a gift and not a performance.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the visit in the Book of the Heart, no names unless permission is given.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding.&quot; (Proverbs 9:10, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom begins in reverence, not in cleverness. The community that is not awed by God will soon be impressed only by itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read Exodus 31:1–11 slowly and list everything the text says God supplied.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make me quick to listen and slow to be certain.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the list in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Feb 7 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> one thing properly made; one overlooked person visited; one list of supplied gifts.</p>"},{"n":7,"month":"February","title":"The Burden Shared","html":"<h2>Week 7 — The Burden Shared</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> February · <strong>Dates:</strong> Feb 14–20</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And I will take of the spirit which is upon thee, and will put it upon them; and they shall bear the burden of the people with thee, that thou bear it not thyself alone.&quot; (Numbers 11:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Anointing is not consumed by distribution. The work is too large for one pair of hands by design.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Divide January&#x27;s list of needs into plots small enough for one household to own.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me build what will remain when I am gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the allocations in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Bear ye one another&#x27;s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.&quot; (Galatians 6:2, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Burden-bearing is the law of Christ, not an optional ministry.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one burden from another household for a named week — a specific task, not a general offer.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me be patient where I am usually sharp.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the task and the week in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For every house is builded by some man; but he that built all things is God.&quot; (Hebrews 3:4, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> We build because we were built. The worker is not the source of the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence in the Book of the Mind: <em>the work is His; I am assigned to it.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me where I have been wise in my own eyes.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> date it.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Feb 14 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> allocated plots; one burden carried; one sentence of ownership.</p>"},{"n":8,"month":"February","title":"Skilled for the Common Good","html":"<h2>Week 8 — Skilled for the Common Good</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> February · <strong>Dates:</strong> Feb 21–27</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Them hath he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work, of the engraver, and of the cunning workman, and of the embroiderer&quot; (Exodus 35:35, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Skill is given for the common work, not for private distinction.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Pair one skilled person with one unskilled person and complete a small piece of work together.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of God, fill the ordinary tools of this day.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what each contributed, in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work&quot; (2 Corinthians 9:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Generosity is not the spending of a surplus; it is the conversion of what we have into what others need.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Give something you would have kept, to someone who cannot repay.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God who sees Leah, teach me to notice the overlooked.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the act in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.&quot; (Psalm 19:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind&#x27;s work includes what it rehearses when nobody is listening.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Keep a note of every decision made this week that was made to avoid embarrassment.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of counsel, let me seek advice before I act.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the count in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Feb 21 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> one shared work; one costly gift; one honest count.</p>"},{"n":9,"month":"February","title":"Making and Mercy, One Motion","html":"<h2>Week 9 — Making and Mercy, One Motion</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> February · <strong>Dates:</strong> Feb 28 – Mar 6</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he hath put in his heart that he may teach, both he, and Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan.&quot; (Exodus 35:34, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The craft and the teaching belong together. A vision that cannot be handed on is not a vision, it is an accomplishment.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write a one-page instruction for the work you did in February so another household can do it from the shared document.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, free me from the need to be seen as the one who did it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the page in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say?&quot; (Luke 6:46, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The test of love is not language.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose one command you have been reciting and obey it literally this week.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let all my things this day be done in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> which one, and what it cost, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he hath filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship&quot; (Exodus 35:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom, understanding and knowledge are three distinct gifts. Knowledge without understanding is information; understanding without wisdom is cleverness.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Sort February&#x27;s recorded acts into three columns: what we knew, what we understood, what we wisely did.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let my mind dwell on what is true and pure.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the sorting in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Feb 28 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>First Re-fire week.</strong> This is the collapse point: where the work has gone quiet, write a smaller deliverable finishable in seven days and pair with someone still moving.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Feb 28):</strong> read aloud the first list of works the community believes God has given it to make. Each work must have one owner, one date and one mercy component. A work without a mercy component is returned to the Book of the Hand for revision.**</p>"},{"n":10,"month":"March","title":"The Pen of a Ready Writer","html":"<h2>Week 10 — The Pen of a Ready Writer</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> March · <strong>Dates:</strong> Mar 7–13</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;My heart is inditing a good matter&quot; (Psalm 45:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The first draft of any vision is written in the heart before it is written on paper.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Each household writes the one sentence it believes God is saying to the community this year. Place it in the shared document without a name attached.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker, let my making be a form of worship, not a form of self.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the sentence in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.&quot; (Matthew 12:34, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Speech is a diagnostic instrument. What a community talks about when it is unguarded tells you what it loves.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> For one meal or one household chat, notice what you talk about without prompting. Write it down honestly.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, let my love be in deed and in truth, not in tongue.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the observation in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But we have the mind of Christ.&quot; (1 Corinthians 2:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind of Christ is not a mood; it is a way of judging.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one decision the community made in January and ask: would this decision have made sense to Jesus? Write the reasoning.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep me from self-deception about what I have heard and not done.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Mar 7 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> one sentence from each household; one speech observation; one decision re-examined.</p>"},{"n":11,"month":"March","title":"What the Mouth Speaks","html":"<h2>Week 11 — What the Mouth Speaks</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> March · <strong>Dates:</strong> Mar 14–20</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.&quot; (Matthew 5:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The work is visible; the glory is not ours.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Finish one unfinished thing from February and share it where your neighbourhood can see it — a public post, a shared link, or a physical place.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me the stone the builders refused.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the finished thing in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.&quot; (Proverbs 15:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The heart is guarded at the point of speech.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> In one difficult conversation this week, answer softly on purpose.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, keep me from rivalry and make me glad of another&#x27;s gift.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what happened, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;He that answereth a matter before he heareth it, it is folly and shame unto him.&quot; (Proverbs 18:13, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom requires hearing before answering.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> In one conversation, ask two questions before offering any opinion.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let reverent fear be the beginning of my knowing.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what you heard that you would have missed, in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Mar 14 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a finished visible work; a soft answer; two questions before an opinion.</p>"},{"n":12,"month":"March","title":"The Vineyard God Planted","html":"<h2>Week 12 — The Vineyard God Planted</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> March · <strong>Dates:</strong> Mar 21–27</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For the vineyard of the LORD of hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant&quot; (Isaiah 5:7, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The work belongs to God before it belongs to us. We are tenants, not owners.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Survey one area of the community&#x27;s life that has been neglected and write what it would take to tend it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, give me a heart that indites before my hand attempts.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the survey in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.&quot; (Matthew 9:36, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Compassion is what vision looks like before it has a plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Spend one hour with someone who is scattered — listen, do not fix.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let mercy outrank ritual in all I do today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> one sentence about what you saw, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature.&quot; (Mark 16:15, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The vision has no right to stay local if the command does not.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down the one group in your area the community has never intentionally approached.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the mind of Christ, give me a mind that empties itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the name in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Mar 21 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a neglected-area survey; one hour of listening; one unapproached group named.</p>"},{"n":13,"month":"March","title":"Counting the Cost","html":"<h2>Week 13 — Counting the Cost</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> March · <strong>Dates:</strong> Mar 28 – Apr 3</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost&quot; (Luke 14:28, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> A costed vision is more spiritual than an unpaid one.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Put real numbers against the Vision Draft: hours, money, people, months.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let this work be done as to You, and not as to men.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the numbers in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so them also which sleep in Jesus will God bring with him.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 4:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Christian hope is not denial of loss. It is the reason we can spend ourselves without despair.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Be with one person who is grieving — in person, by call or by message — and say nothing that tries to explain it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me a soft answer where wrath would be easy.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the visit in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.&quot; (Philippians 1:21, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind that can say this is free from the need to protect its own significance.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one thing you are afraid of losing if the vision succeeds.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me prove Your will instead of presuming it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind, dated.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Mar 28 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Mar 28):</strong> the Vision Draft is read aloud from the Book of the Hand. It must be one page, dated, with real numbers and at least one named mercy component. It is not yet adopted — it is laid on the table for April&#x27;s cost-counting.**</p>"},{"n":14,"month":"April","title":"All to His Glory","html":"<h2>Week 14 — All to His Glory</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> April · <strong>Dates:</strong> Apr 4–10</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Whether therefore ye eat, or drink, or whatsoever ye do, do all to the glory of God.&quot; (1 Corinthians 10:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Hand has no private zone.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Audit one full weekday hour by hour and mark which hours were done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the harvest, make me faithful over what is already in my hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the audit in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men&quot; (Colossians 3:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The audience changes everything. Work done for an audience is exhausting; work done as to the Lord is free.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one task this week with no possibility of being thanked, and do it well.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the Samaritan, make me the neighbour, not the passer-by.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the task in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God and the Father by him.&quot; (Colossians 3:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The name of Jesus is the boundary of a Christian vision.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one line of the Vision Draft and ask whether it could be done in His name without embarrassment.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep my peace stayed on You.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the answer in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Apr 4 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a one-day audit; unseen work; one line tested.</p>"},{"n":15,"month":"April","title":"The Living Sacrifice","html":"<h2>Week 15 — The Living Sacrifice</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> April · <strong>Dates:</strong> Apr 11–17</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.&quot; (Romans 12:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Presented once, the sacrifice walks off the altar — so it must be presented again.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Begin the daily three-minute presentation: hands, heart, mind, named before the day starts.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, count the cost with me and keep me from building on a lie.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the first seven days in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind&quot; (Romans 12:2, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Note the order: the body is presented first; the mind is renewed second.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Identify one pattern in your household you have stopped noticing because it is normal. Name it in the shared document.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me lay down something for the brethren today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.&quot; (Romans 12:2, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The renewed mind is for proving — testing — the will of God, not for receiving a feeling about it.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one belief about the church&#x27;s future that you have never tested against Scripture.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let what I know become what I do.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the belief and the passage you will use, in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Apr 11 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a daily presentation begun; a normal pattern named; an untested belief written.</p>"},{"n":16,"month":"April","title":"Presenting the Body","html":"<h2>Week 16 — Presenting the Body</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> April · <strong>Dates:</strong> Apr 18–24</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them.&quot; (Ephesians 2:10, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The works are prepared; the walking is ours.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Match each household to one prepared work from February&#x27;s list.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, teach my hands the work You prepared for them.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the match in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work&quot; (2 Corinthians 9:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Sufficiency is for abounding, not for accumulating.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Commit a specific portion of income to the year&#x27;s work, and write the number down.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, pour Your love into the places I have kept sealed.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the number in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And let them make me a sanctuary; that I may dwell among them.&quot; (Exodus 25:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The purpose of the work is presence, not productivity.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask: if the work succeeds, will God be more present among us, or only busier?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of truth, correct the story I tell myself about myself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the question and answer in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Apr 18 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a household matched to a work; a stated portion; a presence-test.</p>"},{"n":17,"month":"April","title":"The Merciful Version","html":"<h2>Week 17 — The Merciful Version</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> April · <strong>Dates:</strong> Apr 25 – May 1</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the king shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.&quot; (Matthew 25:40, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> There is no version of the work that bypasses the least.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Redesign one planned work so that it directly benefits someone the community would not naturally choose.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord of the work, fill my hands with skill I did not earn, and let nothing I make be made for applause.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the redesign in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.&quot; (Psalm 37:21, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Mercy is not an add-on to the vision; it is the test of whether the vision is righteous.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one act of mercy that has no strategic value to the church&#x27;s growth.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, love through me where my affection has run out.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?&quot; (Micah 6:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Justice, mercy and humility are one requirement, not three options.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Score the Vision Draft honestly on all three, 1–10, with a sentence for each.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, I lack wisdom; give it without reproach.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the scoring in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Apr 25 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Apr 25):</strong> the <strong>Costed Vision</strong> is adopted for the quarter: time, money, people and the merciful component all named. The first quarter ends with the community able to say what it is for, what it costs and who it is for.**</p>"},{"n":18,"month":"May","title":"The Operator","html":"<h2>Week 18 — The Operator</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> May · <strong>Dates:</strong> May 2–8</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Let all your things be done with charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 16:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Charity does not decorate the work; it governs it.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one work adopted in April and ask what would have to change if love, not efficiency, were the measure.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker of all things, let my plan begin where Yours already is.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the change in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For God is love.&quot; (1 John 4:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is not first a command but a nature. We love because love has acted toward us.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Spend ten minutes naming, specifically, what God has done for you this year.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, give me the measure of Your love for someone hard to love.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> one sentence in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;We love him, because he first loved us.&quot; (1 John 4:19, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The order is not negotiable. Every Christian account of love begins with God&#x27;s prior act.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the order at the head of the Book of the Mind: <em>He first, then we.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let me lean on You and not on my own understanding.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> date it.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday May 2 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a work re-governed; one act named; the order written.</p>"},{"n":19,"month":"May","title":"Charity in the Household","html":"<h2>Week 19 — Charity in the Household</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> May · <strong>Dates:</strong> May 9–15</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men&quot; (Colossians 3:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The first test of a vision is at home.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Improve one thing in your household this week that nobody outside your household will ever see.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me courage to start small and finish truly.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Fathers, provoke not your children to anger, lest they be discouraged.&quot; (Colossians 3:21, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is measured by what it refuses to do as much as by what it does.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one pattern in your household that discourages someone, and stop it for seven days.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of mercy, let my kindness be costly and real.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the pattern and the seven dates in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;He that is slow to anger is better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh a city.&quot; (Proverbs 16:32, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Self-command is a wisdom achievement, not a personality trait.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Keep a tally this week of the moments you governed your temper and the moments it governed you.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, renew my mind after Christ, not after the age.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the tally in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday May 9 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an unseen household improvement; a stopped pattern; a temper tally.</p>"},{"n":20,"month":"May","title":"The Way of the Cross","html":"<h2>Week 20 — The Way of the Cross</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> May · <strong>Dates:</strong> May 16–22</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.&quot; (Matthew 16:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The cross is not an ornament on a vision; it is the shape of it.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose one thing the community would have to give up if it truly followed the adopted vision.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let the work of my hands serve someone I would not have chosen.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you.&quot; (John 15:12, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The measure is His love, not our capacity.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one thing for someone in the community that you would not have done if you had never heard this verse.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, unite my divided heart to fear Your name.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it.&quot; (Matthew 16:25, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The calculus of the kingdom reverses the calculus of the age.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down what you are most unwilling to lose, and what that reveals about your vision.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth, take every thought captive to Your Son.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday May 16 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a named cost; a commanded act; an honest unwillingness.</p>"},{"n":21,"month":"May","title":"Love's Tests","html":"<h2>Week 21 — Love&#x27;s Tests</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> May · <strong>Dates:</strong> May 23–29</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And though I bestow all my goods to feed the poor, and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:3, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Even heroism is profitless without love. The Hand must be examined.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Audit one of the community&#x27;s most admired works for motive: why is it admired, and by whom?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, make my work honest when no one is watching.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the audit in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:4, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is described by behaviour, not by feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask one person who knows you well which phrase in this verse is least true of you. Listen without defending.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me see the person I have been treating as scenery.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what you heard, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Charity never faileth&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Everything else in the list of gifts is temporary. This is the one that remains.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence: <em>if the work fails in five years, what will remain?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me hear before I answer.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday May 23 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a motive audit; a hard question answered; a sentence about what remains.</p>"},{"n":22,"month":"May","title":"The Month of Visitation","html":"<h2>Week 22 — The Month of Visitation</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> May · <strong>Dates:</strong> May 30 – Jun 5</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.&quot; (Psalm 90:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The work of building is sustained by a life that is not ruled by appetite.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Set one boundary on the year&#x27;s work that protects the household from being consumed.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the wilderness, cut a road where I can see none.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the boundary in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.&quot; (James 1:27, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Visitation is not a programme; it is the definition of religion in this passage.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Visit one person in affliction each week of May. Write the number of visits, not the stories.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make my hospitality a gift and not a performance.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the count in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;What doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?&quot; (Micah 6:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The month&#x27;s mercy must be joined to justice and humility or it becomes display.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Review the May visits: which were done to be seen?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make me quick to listen and slow to be certain.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the honest answer in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday May 30 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>SECOND WIND — mandatory for the whole community.</strong> Name that most January resolutions are already dead; re-count the cost; discard one commitment; re-declare one smaller deliverable for the second half; refresh pairs; pray 2 Timothy 1:6.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (May 30):</strong> the <strong>Mercy Map</strong> of the neighbourhood is posted in the shared document: who is hurting, who is isolated, who is unseen, and which household is assigned to each. Every future work in the year must name its mercy component on this map.**</p>"},{"n":23,"month":"June","title":"The First Commandment","html":"<h2>Week 23 — The First Commandment</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> June · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jun 6–12</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.&quot; (Mark 12:30, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The greatest command takes the whole person. No faculty is exempt.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Draw three columns — Hand, Heart, Mind — and write one thing God is asking of each this month.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me build what will remain when I am gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the columns in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the second is like, namely this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is none other commandment greater than these.&quot; (Mark 12:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love of God and love of neighbour are not two separate duties.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one thing this week that is simultaneously love of God and love of a neighbour.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me be patient where I am usually sharp.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the scribe said unto him, Well, Master, thou hast said the truth: for there is one God; and there is none other but he&quot; (Mark 12:32, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The unity of God is the ground of the undivided life.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence: <em>because God is one, I cannot divide my loyalty.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me where I have been wise in my own eyes.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jun 6 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>SECOND WIND — mandatory for the whole community.</strong> Name that most January resolutions are already dead; re-count the cost; discard one commitment; re-declare one smaller deliverable for the second half; refresh pairs; pray 2 Timothy 1:6.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a three-column assignment; a double-love act; a sentence of loyalty.</p>"},{"n":24,"month":"June","title":"Every Seat, One Verb","html":"<h2>Week 24 — Every Seat, One Verb</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> June · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jun 13–19</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength&quot; (Mark 12:33, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Jesus names the seats explicitly. This is not a metaphor imported from elsewhere.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take the three columns from last week and write a single verb that governs all three.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of God, fill the ordinary tools of this day.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the verb in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And to love his neighbour as himself, is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.&quot; (Mark 12:33, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Mercy outranks ritual. The community that sacrifices without loving has misunderstood the command.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one act of mercy in place of one religious observance this week.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God who sees Leah, teach me to notice the overlooked.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the exchange in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And when Jesus saw that he answered discreetly, he said unto him, Thou art not far from the kingdom of God.&quot; (Mark 12:34, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Discretion — wise judgement — is itself near to the kingdom.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down the wisest decision the community made this month and why it was wise.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of counsel, let me seek advice before I act.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jun 13 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a governing verb; mercy over ritual; a wise decision recorded.</p>"},{"n":25,"month":"June","title":"Guarding the Affections","html":"<h2>Week 25 — Guarding the Affections</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> June · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jun 20–26</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.&quot; (Proverbs 4:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The heart is guarded because everything else flows from it.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Identify one input you allow daily that is quietly forming your affections against love.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, free me from the need to be seen as the one who did it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Unite my heart to fear thy name.&quot; (Psalm 86:11, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> This is the hinge prayer of the whole book: the prayer against a divided heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Pray this verse aloud each morning this week, once, before anything else.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let all my things this day be done in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the seven mornings in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;The heart is deceitful above all things, and desperately wicked: who can know it?&quot; (Jeremiah 17:9, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The diagnosis is severe, but it is not the end of the passage or of the book.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read 1 John 3:20 alongside Jeremiah 17:9 and write the two verses side by side in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let my mind dwell on what is true and pure.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> them there.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jun 20 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an input named; a prayer repeated; two verses held together.</p>"},{"n":26,"month":"June","title":"The Covenant of the Whole Person","html":"<h2>Week 26 — The Covenant of the Whole Person</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> June · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jun 27 – Jul 3</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Paul prays for wholeness, not for improvement in one faculty.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Draft the Covenant of the Whole Person: one commitment each for Hand, Heart and Mind, with a date.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker, let my making be a form of worship, not a form of self.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the draft in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Faithful is he that calleth you, who also will do it.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The covenant rests on God&#x27;s faithfulness, not on ours.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Add your name to the covenant in the shared document, together as a community, not as individuals only.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, let my love be in deed and in truth, not in tongue.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the signing in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you.&quot; (1 Peter 5:10, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Perfection and stability are His work after suffering, not instant achievements.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence about what the community has suffered this year and what it has learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep me from self-deception about what I have heard and not done.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jun 27 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>High-alert week.</strong> The first fade and the mid-year death zone are where resolutions die. Watch for silence before it becomes resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Jun 27):</strong> the Covenant of the Whole Person is read in the online gathering and signed in the shared document. The second quarter ends with a community that has counted the cost, tested its mercy and bound all three faculties under one promise.**</p>"},{"n":27,"month":"July","title":"Not in Word Only","html":"<h2>Week 27 — Not in Word Only</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> July · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jul 4–10</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue; but in deed and in truth.&quot; (1 John 3:18, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The month&#x27;s work is the conversion of language into action.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one phrase the community says often and turn it into a scheduled act.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me the stone the builders refused.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the phrase and the act in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Hereby perceive we the love of God, because he laid down his life for us: and we ought to lay down our lives for the brethren.&quot; (1 John 3:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The measure of love is life laid down, not comfort increased.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Give one day this month to someone else&#x27;s need at your own cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, keep me from rivalry and make me glad of another&#x27;s gift.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the day and what it cost, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But whoso hath this world&#x27;s good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him?&quot; (1 John 3:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The question is not whether we have enough, but whether our compassion closes when we see need.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down one need you have seen this month and done nothing about.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let reverent fear be the beginning of my knowing.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jul 4 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a phrase turned into an act; a costly day; a need owned.</p>"},{"n":28,"month":"July","title":"The Good Samaritan Road","html":"<h2>Week 28 — The Good Samaritan Road</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> July · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jul 11–17</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But a certain Samaritan, as he journeyed, came where he was: and when he saw him, he had compassion on him&quot; (Luke 10:33, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Mercy is discovered on a journey, not in a committee room.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose one route you travel regularly and make it a mercy route — one intentional stop each week.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, give me a heart that indites before my hand attempts.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the route and the stops in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And went to him, and bound up his wounds, pouring in oil and wine, and set him on his own beast, and brought him to an inn, and took care of him.&quot; (Luke 10:34, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Compassion that stops at feeling is incomplete. The Samaritan&#x27;s love had a budget and a schedule.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Provide something concrete and ongoing for one person — not a one-off.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let mercy outrank ritual in all I do today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the commitment in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Which now of these three, thinkest thou, was neighbour unto him that fell among the thieves?&quot; (Luke 10:36, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Jesus ends with a question, not a verdict. The community must answer it for itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write your answer with a name in it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the mind of Christ, give me a mind that empties itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jul 11 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a mercy route; an ongoing provision; a named neighbour.</p>"},{"n":29,"month":"July","title":"The Feast Without Invitation","html":"<h2>Week 29 — The Feast Without Invitation</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> July · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jul 18–24</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.&quot; (Matthew 16:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Hospitality without self-denial is entertainment.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Host a meal for people who cannot reciprocate — around your own table or a shared video table. Keep the guest list small and intentional.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let this work be done as to You, and not as to men.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the meal in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But when thou makest a feast, call the poor, the maimed, the lame, the blind&quot; (Luke 14:13, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The guest list is a theological statement.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Invite one person from the Mercy Map to the meal.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me a soft answer where wrath would be easy.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the invitation in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And thou shalt be blessed; for they cannot recompense thee: for thou shalt be recompensed at the resurrection of the just.&quot; (Luke 14:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The promise is eschatological. We give now because the account is not closed.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence about what you expect God to do that you cannot see yet.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me prove Your will instead of presuming it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jul 18 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a meal; a specific invitation; a sentence of hope.</p>"},{"n":30,"month":"July","title":"Mercy That Builds","html":"<h2>Week 30 — Mercy That Builds</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> July · <strong>Dates:</strong> Jul 25–31</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And I will take of the spirit which is upon thee, and will put it upon them; and they shall bear the burden of the people with thee, that thou bear it not thyself alone.&quot; (Numbers 11:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Mercy that can only be done by one person is not a vision; it is a heroics project.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Hand one July work over to another household entirely.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the harvest, make me faithful over what is already in my hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the transfer in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.&quot; (Galatians 6:9, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Perseverance in mercy is a fruit of the Spirit, not a personality strength.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one mercy work you wanted to quit and recommit for one more month.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the Samaritan, make me the neighbour, not the passer-by.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the recommitment in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;As we have therefore opportunity, let us do good unto all men, especially unto them who are of the household of faith.&quot; (Galatians 6:10, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> There is a priority within the universality: the household of faith first, but not only.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Review the month&#x27;s acts: were any restricted to people exactly like us?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep my peace stayed on You.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the honest answer in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Jul 25 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Jul 25):</strong> the <strong>first completed work of mercy</strong> is presented with evidence — what was done, for whom, over how long, and what it cost. Evidence is required; intentions are not accepted.**</p>"},{"n":31,"month":"August","title":"Charity Never Faileth","html":"<h2>Week 31 — Charity Never Faileth</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> August · <strong>Dates:</strong> Aug 1–7</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:13, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The greatest is not the most useful. It is the one that remains.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Rank the year&#x27;s works by what will remain when the building is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, count the cost with me and keep me from building on a lie.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the ranking in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Charity never faileth: but whether there be prophecies, they shall fail; whether there be tongues, they shall cease; whether there be knowledge, it shall vanish away.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Even knowledge is temporary. This is a hard word for a year that includes a Wisdom pillar.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one thing you know that you will not know in twenty years, and one thing love will still be doing.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me lay down something for the brethren today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> both in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For we know in part, and we prophesy in part.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:9, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Partial knowledge is the human condition, not a failure of diligence.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down one thing the community was sure of in January that it is less sure of now.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let what I know become what I do.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Aug 1 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a ranking by permanence; a contrast between knowledge and love; a revised certainty.</p>"},{"n":32,"month":"August","title":"The More Excellent Way","html":"<h2>Week 32 — The More Excellent Way</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> August · <strong>Dates:</strong> Aug 8–14</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;and yet shew I unto you a more excellent way.&quot; (1 Corinthians 12:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The way is shown, not earned. It is more excellent than the best gifts.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take the community&#x27;s most impressive gift or resource and ask where love would put it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, teach my hands the work You prepared for them.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the answer in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Excellence without love is noise.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Identify one thing the community does well that has become noise.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, pour Your love into the places I have kept sealed.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And though I have the gift of prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:2, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Paul is willing to call knowledge nothing if love is absent.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence: <em>what we know is only useful if…</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of truth, correct the story I tell myself about myself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Aug 8 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a gift re-placed; a noise named; a sentence about knowledge.</p>"},{"n":33,"month":"August","title":"What Love Outlasts","html":"<h2>Week 33 — What Love Outlasts</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> August · <strong>Dates:</strong> Aug 15–21</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And though I bestow all my goods to feed the poor, and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:3, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Even the most costly giving can be empty.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Audit one act of generosity from the year: what was the motive underneath it?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord of the work, fill my hands with skill I did not earn, and let nothing I make be made for applause.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the audit in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:4, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Patience and kindness are the first two marks. They are cheap to admire and expensive to practise.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Practise one deliberate act of patience this week with someone who usually tries you.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, love through me where my affection has run out.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:13, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Faith and hope remain too. Love is greater because it is the nature of God, not only a response to Him.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence explaining why love, not faith or hope, is the greatest.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, I lack wisdom; give it without reproach.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Aug 15 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a generosity audit; an act of patience; a sentence of reasoning.</p>"},{"n":34,"month":"August","title":"The Refusal of Rivalry","html":"<h2>Week 34 — The Refusal of Rivalry</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> August · <strong>Dates:</strong> Aug 22–28</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.&quot; (James 3:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Rivalry among workers is the great destroyer of a common vision.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Pair two households that have been quietly competing and give them one shared task.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker of all things, let my plan begin where Yours already is.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the pairing in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits&quot; (James 3:17, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom from above is described in relational terms.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Speak well of someone you would normally compete with, in the group chat or in their absence.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, give me the measure of Your love for someone hard to love.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the act in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.&quot; (James 3:18, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Peace is not the absence of conflict; it is the seedbed of righteousness.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one unresolved conflict in the community and write what a peaceful resolution would require.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let me lean on You and not on my own understanding.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Aug 22 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a shared task; a spoken good; a conflict mapped.</p>"},{"n":35,"month":"August","title":"Love's Permanence","html":"<h2>Week 35 — Love&#x27;s Permanence</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> August · <strong>Dates:</strong> Aug 29 – Sep 4</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Charity never faileth&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The community&#x27;s works will be tested by permanence.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose the one work from the year you would keep if all others were removed, and say why.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me courage to start small and finish truly.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;God is love; and he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, and God in him.&quot; (1 John 4:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is not only something we do; it is where we dwell.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Spend one hour this week in the presence of someone you would rather avoid.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of mercy, let my kindness be costly and real.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what you noticed, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us.&quot; (1 John 4:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Knowing and believing are both required.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the difference between knowing about God&#x27;s love and believing it for yourself.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, renew my mind after Christ, not after the age.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Aug 29 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>QUARTER MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Aug 29):</strong> the <strong>More Excellent Way</strong> is published: every work of the year reordered under love, with the works that were merely admired marked as such. The second quarter ends with the community able to say not only what it built, but why it built it.**</p>"},{"n":36,"month":"September","title":"Ask Without Doubting","html":"<h2>Week 36 — Ask Without Doubting</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> September · <strong>Dates:</strong> Sep 5–11</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.&quot; (James 1:5, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Asking is not a sign of weakness but the entry to wisdom.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the community&#x27;s three hardest questions at the head of the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let the work of my hands serve someone I would not have chosen.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> them there, dated.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And if a kingdom be divided against itself, that kingdom cannot stand.&quot; (Mark 3:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Division is the great threat to a work; love is the only binding agent.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask one person from a different household what they believe the community&#x27;s real division is.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, unite my divided heart to fear Your name.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what you heard, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.&quot; (James 1:6, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wavering is not doubt about God&#x27;s existence; it is divided loyalty about His goodness.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one area where the community asks God and then proceeds as though He had not answered.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth, take every thought captive to Your Son.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Sep 5 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> three hard questions; a division named; an area of wavering owned.</p>"},{"n":37,"month":"September","title":"The Fear of the Lord","html":"<h2>Week 37 — The Fear of the Lord</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> September · <strong>Dates:</strong> Sep 12–18</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding.&quot; (Proverbs 9:10, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Reverence is not the opposite of confidence; it is the foundation of it.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Review the year&#x27;s works for anything done in a spirit of casualness toward God.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, make my work honest when no one is watching.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the tables were the work of God, and the writing was the writing of God, graven upon the tables.&quot; (Exodus 32:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The fear of the Lord includes a refusal to treat His words as negotiable.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Keep one command this week that you would normally reinterpret.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me see the person I have been treating as scenery.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> which one, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And unto man he said, Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom; and to depart from evil is understanding.&quot; (Job 28:28, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom and understanding are defined together; departure from evil is not optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one practice the community has tolerated that should be departed from.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me hear before I answer.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Sep 12 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> casualness examined; a command kept; a practice named for departure.</p>"},{"n":38,"month":"September","title":"The Mind of Christ","html":"<h2>Week 38 — The Mind of Christ</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> September · <strong>Dates:</strong> Sep 19–25</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For who hath known the mind of the Lord, that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Christ.&quot; (1 Corinthians 2:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind of Christ is given, not achieved by study alone.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Take one decision from the Book of the Mind and rewrite it as if Christ were present in the online meeting.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the wilderness, cut a road where I can see none.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the rewrite in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Let this mind be in you, which was also in Christ Jesus&quot; (Philippians 2:5, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The mind that empties itself is the mind that builds.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Give up one position you have been defending in the community.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make my hospitality a gift and not a performance.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the position and what you gained, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Who, being in the form of God, thought it not robbery to be equal with God&quot; (Philippians 2:6, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The pattern of Christ&#x27;s mind is downward movement, not upward grasping.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one way the community&#x27;s vision has become about upward grasping.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, make me quick to listen and slow to be certain.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Sep 19 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a decision rewritten; a position released; a grasping named.</p>"},{"n":39,"month":"September","title":"Doers, Not Hearers","html":"<h2>Week 39 — Doers, Not Hearers</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> September · <strong>Dates:</strong> Sep 26 – Oct 2</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.&quot; (James 1:22, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The judgement on hearing without doing is self-deception.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Choose one passage the community has heard often and obey it literally this week.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me build what will remain when I am gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the passage and the act in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass&quot; (James 1:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Hearing without doing produces a false self-image.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask someone: what is one thing I say but do not do?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me be patient where I am usually sharp.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the answer in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.&quot; (James 1:25, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Blessing is attached to the deed, not the hearing.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one line in the Book of the Mind: <em>this year I heard much; I did…</em> and complete it honestly.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me where I have been wise in my own eyes.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Sep 26 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Sep 26):</strong> the <strong>Discernment Register</strong> is opened with the year&#x27;s first formal correction: one thing the community will stop, one thing it will start, one thing it will keep. The third quarter begins with Wisdom governing the review.**</p>"},{"n":40,"month":"October","title":"Trust and Lean Not","html":"<h2>Week 40 — Trust and Lean Not</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> October · <strong>Dates:</strong> Oct 3–9</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.&quot; (Proverbs 3:5, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Hand is built on a trust it did not manufacture.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Review the Costed Vision: which part relies entirely on your own understanding?</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of God, fill the ordinary tools of this day.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.&quot; (Proverbs 3:6, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Acknowledging God in <em>all</em> ways removes the sacred/secular split from decisions.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask God&#x27;s direction on one ordinary decision this week, out loud.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God who sees Leah, teach me to notice the overlooked.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what happened, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the LORD, and depart from evil.&quot; (Proverbs 3:7, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The beginning of folly is the conviction that you are wise.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write down the last time you were certain and wrong.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of counsel, let me seek advice before I act.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Oct 3 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a self-reliant portion named; God acknowledged in an ordinary decision; a remembered error.</p>"},{"n":41,"month":"October","title":"The Counsellors","html":"<h2>Week 41 — The Counsellors</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> October · <strong>Dates:</strong> Oct 10–16</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.&quot; (Proverbs 11:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> A vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Invite someone outside the community to critique the Vision Draft.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, free me from the need to be seen as the one who did it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the critique in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;He that walketh with wise men shall be wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed.&quot; (Proverbs 13:20, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Companionship forms the heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Spend one hour this week with someone wiser than you, asking rather than telling.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let all my things this day be done in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> what you learned, in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;A wise man feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool rageth, and is confident.&quot; (Proverbs 14:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Confidence is not the mark of wisdom; fear and departure are.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one thing in the vision that feels confident but has not been examined.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let my mind dwell on what is true and pure.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Oct 10 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an outside critique; an hour with a wise person; an unexamined confidence.</p>"},{"n":42,"month":"October","title":"Wisdom in the Gate","html":"<h2>Week 42 — Wisdom in the Gate</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> October · <strong>Dates:</strong> Oct 17–23</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth her voice in the streets&quot; (Proverbs 1:20, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Wisdom is public. A vision that only makes sense inside the online meeting is not yet wisdom.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Explain the year&#x27;s vision to someone outside the community in one minute, without church vocabulary.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker, let my making be a form of worship, not a form of self.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> how it landed, in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded&quot; (Proverbs 1:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love can be refused. The community must ask whether it has been deaf.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one invitation from God this year you have declined.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, let my love be in deed and in truth, not in tongue.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell safely, and shall be quiet from fear of evil.&quot; (Proverbs 1:33, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Safety and quiet are the promise to the one who listens.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one fear the community has carried this year and what it would look like to be quiet from it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep me from self-deception about what I have heard and not done.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Oct 17 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a one-minute public explanation; a refused invitation; a fear examined.</p>"},{"n":43,"month":"October","title":"The Stone the Builders Refused","html":"<h2>Week 43 — The Stone the Builders Refused</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> October · <strong>Dates:</strong> Oct 24–30</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;The stone which the builders refused is become the head stone of the corner.&quot; (Psalm 118:22, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The most important element of a work is often the one the builders dismissed.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Identify something the community overlooked in January that now looks essential.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, show me the stone the builders refused.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;This is the LORD&#x27;s doing; it is marvellous in our eyes.&quot; (Psalm 118:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The work is His before it is ours; wonder is the proper response.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one thing this week purely because it is good, with no measurable outcome.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, keep me from rivalry and make me glad of another&#x27;s gift.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;This is the day which the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.&quot; (Psalm 118:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The day is received before it is used.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Begin each morning this week with this verse before looking at the plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let reverent fear be the beginning of my knowing.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the seven mornings in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Oct 24 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an overlooked stone found; an unmeasured good; a received day.</p>"},{"n":44,"month":"October","title":"Discernment in the Marketplace","html":"<h2>Week 44 — Discernment in the Marketplace</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> October · <strong>Dates:</strong> Oct 31 – Nov 6</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the king shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.&quot; (Matthew 25:40, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Every economic decision is also a decision about Christ&#x27;s brothers.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Audit one purchase or budget line of the year against this verse.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, give me a heart that indites before my hand attempts.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the audit in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in&quot; (Matthew 25:35, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The works of mercy are concrete and unnamed in their recipient.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one of these six things this week without knowing the recipient&#x27;s name.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let mercy outrank ritual in all I do today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the category and the act in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Then shall the king say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world&quot; (Matthew 25:34, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The verdict is based on what was done, not on what was known.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence: <em>what will the year&#x27;s record actually show?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the mind of Christ, give me a mind that empties itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Oct 31 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Oct 31):</strong> the <strong>Reviewed Vision</strong> is read in ink. It differs from April&#x27;s version. The differences are listed explicitly: what was removed, what was added, what was reordered. A vision that survives a year unchanged has probably not been reviewed.**</p>"},{"n":45,"month":"November","title":"The Checked Cost","html":"<h2>Week 45 — The Checked Cost</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> November · <strong>Dates:</strong> Nov 7–13</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost&quot; (Luke 14:28, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The cost was counted in January; now it must be checked.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Compare January&#x27;s estimate with November&#x27;s actual expenditure of time, money and people.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what remains when the work is gone; love keeps, wisdom judges.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let this work be done as to You, and not as to men.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> both columns in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Or what king, going to make war against another king, sitteth not down first, and consulteth whether he be able with ten thousand to meet him that cometh against him with twenty thousand?&quot; (Luke 14:31, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love does not exempt us from strategic honesty.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name one commitment the community cannot honour and release it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let this act be both a work of mercy and a work of skill, done as to the Lord.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me a soft answer where wrath would be easy.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the release in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;So likewise, whosoever he be of you that forsaketh not all that he hath, he cannot be my disciple.&quot; (Luke 14:33, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The closing verse of the passage is the hardest. It is the measure of discipleship, not of project success.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write what you have actually forsaken this year, not what you intended to.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask what you would change if you had to do this week again in charity.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me prove Your will instead of presuming it.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Nov 7 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> two columns of cost; a commitment released; an honest inventory.</p>"},{"n":46,"month":"November","title":"The Whole Person Before God","html":"<h2>Week 46 — The Whole Person Before God</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> November · <strong>Dates:</strong> Nov 14–20</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year began with a gift; it ends with the same prayer.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read the three Vision Books side by side and mark where Hand, Heart and Mind agree and where they do not.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Build with mercy built in — a work that helps no one is not yet the work.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the harvest, make me faithful over what is already in my hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the marks in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.&quot; (James 4:8, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The condition named is not weakness but double-mindedness.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Each household names the one area where it has been double-minded all year.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Refuse the strategic calculation: do good because it is good, then examine what it taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of the Samaritan, make me the neighbour, not the passer-by.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart, without explanation.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The prayer is addressed to God, not to the will.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the year&#x27;s one-sentence testimony: <em>what God did in me through this year.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let wisdom be proved by the hand; a lesson never acted on was never learned.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, keep my peace stayed on You.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Nov 14 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an agreement map; a double-mindedness named; a one-sentence testimony.</p>"},{"n":47,"month":"November","title":"The Year's Audit","html":"<h2>Week 47 — The Year&#x27;s Audit</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> November · <strong>Dates:</strong> Nov 21–27</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men&quot; (Colossians 3:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The final audit is of manner, not only of result.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read the Book of the Hand and mark every act that was done for an audience.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take counsel before you act; a vision without counsel is a fall waiting to happen.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, count the cost with me and keep me from building on a lie.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the count in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 13:13, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> At the end of the year, only one measurement finally matters.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Ask five people: <em>has this community loved me well this year?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do it in deed and in truth, not in tongue; and count what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let me lay down something for the brethren today.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the answers in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.&quot; (James 1:22, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year&#x27;s final warning is against self-deception.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the one thing you know about yourself now that you did not know in January.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Hold truth and mercy together: correct the error without shaming the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, let what I know become what I do.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Nov 21 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> an audience-count; five answers; one known thing.</p>"},{"n":48,"month":"November","title":"The Send-Off","html":"<h2>Week 48 — The Send-Off</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> November · <strong>Dates:</strong> Nov 28 – Dec 4</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature.&quot; (Mark 16:15, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> A vision that ends inside the community has failed.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Name the one person or place outside the community the 2028 work will be sent to.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let the Great Commandment govern the design: God first, neighbour in the same motion.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, teach my hands the work You prepared for them.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature.&quot; (Mark 16:15, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Sending is an act of love, not an expansion strategy.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Commission one household in the online gathering for the 2028 work, with prayer and no fanfare.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Carry it in patience; love that is hurried is often love that is not loved back.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit, pour Your love into the places I have kept sealed.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the commissioning in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world.&quot; (Matthew 28:20, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The promise of presence is the ground of sending.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence: <em>what I am sending is not what I am keeping.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Review in ink; a vision that survives a year unchanged has not been reviewed.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Spirit of truth, correct the story I tell myself about myself.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Nov 28 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>MONTHLY MILESTONE — Vision Sunday (Nov 28):</strong> the <strong>Year&#x27;s Audit</strong> is read publicly from the Book of the Mind. It includes what failed. Nothing is omitted to protect anyone&#x27;s reputation.**</p>"},{"n":49,"month":"December","title":"The Maker","html":"<h2>Week 49 — The Maker</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> December · <strong>Dates:</strong> Dec 5–11</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.&quot; (John 1:3, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Maker is the one who made the hands that make.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Complete one piece of work begun in January and place it at the centre of your Advent gathering — a household table or a shared video table.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Before you begin, ask who this serves; before you finish, ask what it cost. Love names the person; wisdom counts the price.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord of the work, fill my hands with skill I did not earn, and let nothing I make be made for applause.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible&quot; (Colossians 1:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Love is not an abstraction; it is the Creator entering His creation.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Do one act of hospitality that would have been impossible without the year&#x27;s work.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love supply the person, creativity supply the way, and wisdom supply the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, love through me where my affection has run out.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.&quot; (John 1:1, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Word is a Person before He is a message.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one sentence about the difference between a vision and a Word.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Write what you learned, then turn it into a better act of love on Monday.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, I lack wisdom; give it without reproach.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Dec 5 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a completed first work; a hospitality act; a sentence about the Word.</p>"},{"n":50,"month":"December","title":"The Lover","html":"<h2>Week 50 — The Lover</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> December · <strong>Dates:</strong> Dec 12–18</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son&quot; (John 3:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Giving is the shape of love.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Give away one thing the community made this year, to someone outside it.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Make it as to the Lord, for someone you did not choose, and only after you have counted what it requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Maker of all things, let my plan begin where Yours already is.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you.&quot; (John 15:12, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The measure is still His love.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read the Book of the Heart aloud in small groups and give thanks for what God did through ordinary people.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do not merely feel; make something concrete, and weigh whether it truly helps.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Jesus, give me the measure of Your love for someone hard to love.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the thanksgiving in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;Hereby perceive we the love of God, because he laid down his life for us: and we ought to lay down our lives for the brethren.&quot; (1 John 3:16, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Mind&#x27;s final lesson is that knowledge of love is proved by laying down life.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write one thing in 2028 you are willing to lose for the brethren.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let discernment correct the work, not merely comment on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let me lean on You and not on my own understanding.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Dec 12 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> a gift given away; a thanksgiving; a willingness named.</p>"},{"n":51,"month":"December","title":"The Wisdom of God","html":"<h2>Week 51 — The Wisdom of God</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> December · <strong>Dates:</strong> Dec 19–25</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;But unto them which are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power of God, and the wisdom of God.&quot; (1 Corinthians 1:24, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year&#x27;s three pillars meet in one Person.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Open the three Vision Books together in one online meeting and write a single title across them: <em>Christ, the power of God and the wisdom of God.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let love choose the recipient and wisdom choose the method. Neither is optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, give me courage to start small and finish truly.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the title in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.&quot; (John 1:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The Incarnation is where Hand, Heart and Mind became one life.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Keep the Advent meal simple — around your own table or a shared video table — and begin with five minutes of silence.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Let mercy be specific, well-made and sustainable — not a burst of feeling.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of mercy, let my kindness be costly and real.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the meal in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;For in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily.&quot; (Colossians 2:9, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> Fullness is not distributed among the pillars; it is in Him.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the year&#x27;s closing sentence: <em>what I now believe that I did not believe on January 3.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Judge the week by what love did and what the mind now knows.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, renew my mind after Christ, not after the age.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Dec 19 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>Weekly output:</strong> one title across three books; a shared meal; a closing belief.</p>"},{"n":52,"month":"December","title":"The Manger: All Three in One Person","html":"<h2>Week 52 — The Manger: All Three in One Person</h2>\n<p><strong>Month:</strong> December · <strong>Dates:</strong> Dec 26 – Jan 1</p>\n<p><strong>Rule:</strong> hand on Monday, heart on Wednesday, mind on Friday. Every activity is executed in love and with wisdom. Every session ends in prayer and is recorded.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Monday — Divine Creativity · The Hand</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us&quot; (John 1:14, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year ends where it began: with a gift, not a resolution. The work of 2028 begins from the manger.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What is one thing God is already doing that you had not noticed?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Write the 2028 Vision Draft in one page, using only what the three Books actually contain.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Do the work well, do it unseen if possible, and do not let the applause of others become your motive.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, let the work of my hands serve someone I would not have chosen.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Receive the work as a gift; ask what God is already doing before you plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Name the one decision you are making and the reason for it.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Use your hands this week — make, repair, build or serve something real.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Name who benefits, and who has been left out of the plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Count the cost in money, hours and what you are laying down.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> it in the Book of the Hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Wednesday — Divine Love · The Heart</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And she brought forth her firstborn son, and wrapped him in swaddling clothes, and laid him in a manger&quot; (Luke 2:7, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The greatest work ever done in creation was done in a stable, unseen.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> Who is the person you have been treating as scenery?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Give thanks by name for one person whose unseen work held the community together in 2027.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Ask before you give; wisdom hears the need before love supplies it.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord, unite my divided heart to fear Your name.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Pray for one person by name today; love begins with God&#x27;s prior love.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Test the motive: would you do this if nobody saw it?</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Include one bodily act — a visit, a meal, a hand, a walk, a call.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Serve one person in your household and one outside it.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Give something you would have kept; record what it cost.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> the name in the Book of the Heart.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Friday — Divine Wisdom · The Mind</h4>\n<p><strong>Anchor (KJV):</strong> &quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly. And I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV).</p>\n<p><strong>Teach:</strong> The year closes on a prayer you did not write.</p>\n<p><strong>Interactive — reply in one line:</strong> What do you lack wisdom about right now?</p>\n<p><strong>Creative activity:</strong> Read the prayer aloud together in the online gathering. Sign the 2028 Vision Draft.</p>\n<p><strong>Execute in love and wisdom:</strong> Take the lesson into the Book of the Mind and let it govern the next building.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of truth, take every thought captive to Your Son.</p>\n<p><strong>Reply:</strong> type <em>Amen</em>, or name one person you are praying for.</p>\n<p><strong>Walk the five dimensions in this session:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What this session asks of you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td>Ask for wisdom without wavering; begin with reverent fear.</td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td>Write one thing you now know that you did not know on Monday.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td>Keep the unprogrammed day — rest is commanded, not earned.</td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td>Tell one person what you learned and ask what they think.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Recount the week against the Cost Sheet; correct one figure.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Record:</strong> both in the Book of the Mind.</p>\n<p><strong>Post evidence:</strong> DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE — with a link, a name or a date.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>The four fields — this week</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Weekly deliverable</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong> — hand, heart, mind</td><td>One examination, written</td><td>Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong> — the household</td><td>One thing done together</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> — the one project</td><td>One deliverable with a deadline</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong> — my corner of the country</td><td>One act of honest work, order, mercy, truth or capacity</td><td>Book of the Heart</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resources: <code>../../RESOURCES/12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md</code>, <code>../../RESOURCES/11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Interactive five-dimension check — Friday</h3>\n<p>Rate each 1–5 and type one line of evidence. One correction each.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence this week</th><th>One correction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Resource: <code>../../RESOURCES/13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md</code>.</p>\n<h3>Accountability fire — this week</h3>\n<p><strong>Monday Dec 26 — Declare:</strong> one small deliverable for <strong>each</strong> of the four fields — Self, Family, Business and Nation — each with a deadline, a mercy component and a wisdom check. Use the Four Fields Planner. Post by 12:00.</p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday — Spark:</strong> &quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>Friday — Evidence:</strong> post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.</p>\n<p><strong>If quiet:</strong> 7 days without evidence — pair with another household. 14 days — a shame-free reset conversation. Never treat silence as resignation.</p>\n<p><strong>YEAR MILESTONE — Commissioning Sunday (Dec 26):</strong> the 2028 Vision is sealed from the evidence of the three Books. The community declares together the short declaration:**</p>"}],"resources":[{"slug":"01-PROJECT-CHARTER","title":"01 — PROJECT CHARTER","html":"<h2>01 — PROJECT CHARTER</h2>\n<h4>One project. One page. One year.</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it?&quot; (Luke 14:28, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Fill this in during Weeks 3–4. Do not begin a second project until a quarterly review has released the first.</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Your answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Name of member</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Household / accountability partner</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><strong>The one project</strong> (name it in six words)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The specific people it serves (not &quot;everyone&quot;)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The skill God has already given me for it (Week 2 inventory)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>My KJV anchor for this project</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What will exist by the end of Week 13?</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What will exist by the end of the year?</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Time cost per week (honest hours)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Money cost (honest figure)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Who else carries it with me</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The mercy component — who cannot pay and will still be served</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The wisdom check — what would make me stop and rethink</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What I am laying down to do this one thing</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Date chosen</td><td>/ /2027</td></tr><tr><td>Signature (typed)</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The four tests before you sign</h3>\n<p>1. <strong>Hand:</strong> Can I actually make or deliver this with the skill I have been given? 2. <strong>Heart:</strong> Would I still do it if nobody applauded? Who who is loved through it? 3. <strong>Mind:</strong> Have I counted the cost, and can I explain the decision in one minute to someone outside the community? 4. <strong>Household:</strong> Does my family become more whole through this, or less?</p>\n<h3>The rule</h3>\n<p>One project. If it changes, it is <strong>re-scoped in writing</strong> at a quarterly review or at the Second Wind — never quietly replaced. &quot;And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not&quot; (Galatians 6:9, KJV).</p>"},{"slug":"02-FAMILY-RULE-OF-LIFE","title":"02 — FAMILY RULE OF LIFE","html":"<h2>02 — FAMILY RULE OF LIFE</h2>\n<h4>The household is the first field</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;And thou shalt love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might. And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart: And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children&quot; (Deuteronomy 6:5–7, KJV).</blockquote>\n<p><strong>A project that makes a family stranger to itself is not a faithful project.</strong> Fill this in during Week 1 and review it every quarter.</p>\n<h3>Daily — three minutes, before the day starts</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Hand:</strong> &quot;Lord, these hands today — your work.&quot;</li><li><strong>Heart:</strong> &quot;This heart today — your love.&quot;</li><li><strong>Mind:</strong> &quot;This mind today — your truth.&quot;</li><li>One name each for whom the day&#x27;s work will be done.</li></ul>\n<h3>Weekly</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>Family act</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Monday</td><td>Declare the week&#x27;s one deliverable together. Every household member says one sentence.</td><td>Entry in the Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td>Wednesday</td><td>Ask the spark question at the table or in the household chat: <em>what exists now that did not exist on Monday?</em></td><td>Entry in the Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td>Friday</td><td>Post DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE together. No shame if the answer is NOT DONE.</td><td>Entry in the Book of the Mind</td></tr><tr><td>One mercy act</td><td>Feed, visit, call, repair or welcome someone together</td><td>Named in the Book of the Heart</td></tr><tr><td>One project hour</td><td>Work on the single project together, even for sixty minutes</td><td>Book of the Hand</td></tr><tr><td>Sunday</td><td>Worship and rest. No curriculum work.</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Household commitments</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Commitment</th><th>Our answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One evening a week with no project work</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One meal a week with no screens</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One person we will serve together this month</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What we will not trade away for the project</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>How we will handle a dry or tired week</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Who holds us accountable when we go quiet</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Protections</h3>\n<ul><li>The household is <strong>not</strong> a project to optimise. It is the first work of God.</li><li>Do not discuss a member&#x27;s private struggle in the community record.</li><li>&quot;Fathers, provoke not your children to anger, lest they be discouraged&quot; (Colossians 3:21, KJV).</li><li>Tiredness is not failure. &quot;Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while&quot; (Mark 6:31, KJV).</li></ul>"},{"slug":"03-WEEKLY-ACCOUNTABILITY-SHEET","title":"03 — WEEKLY ACCOUNTABILITY SHEET","html":"<h2>03 — WEEKLY ACCOUNTABILITY SHEET</h2>\n<h4>Copy one per week</h4>\n<p><strong>Week ___</strong> · Dates ____________ · Member ____________ · Project ____________</p>\n<h3>Monday — DECLARE (by 12:00)</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One deliverable that will exist by Friday</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Deadline (time, not just day)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Who it serves</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Wisdom check — what would make me stop</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Family member who heard the declaration</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Wednesday — SPARK</h3>\n<p>The fire asks: <strong>&quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>What exists at this moment</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>If nothing: the honest reason in one line</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Friday — EVIDENCE (by 20:00)</h3>\n<p>Tick one:  DONE ☐  PARTIAL ☐  NOT DONE ☐</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The evidence (link, name, photo reference, date)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What remains, if partial</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>New dated deadline, if partial</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What this taught me (one line for the Book of the Mind)</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Fire record (for your eyes, not published)</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Declaration received on time?</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Spark answered?</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Evidence posted?</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Days silent</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Escalation used (message / call / pair / reset)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Re-fire needed?</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<blockquote>&quot;The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.&quot; (Leviticus 6:13, KJV)</blockquote>"},{"slug":"04-COST-SHEET","title":"04 — COST SHEET","html":"<h2>04 — COST SHEET</h2>\n<h4>Count it before you build; count it again in June</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it?&quot; (Luke 14:28, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Use at Week 13, at the Second Wind (Weeks 22–23), and at every quarterly review.</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>January estimate</th><th>Actual now</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hours per week</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Hours per month</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Money required to start</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Money required to sustain</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Skills already present</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Skills still missing</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>People carrying it</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Hours of family time it takes</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What I have stopped doing for this</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The hard questions</h3>\n<p>1. What does this project cost my family that I have not named? 2. What am I hoping this project will do for me that only God can do? 3. If the project fails in twelve months, what remains? 4. Can I finish what is on this sheet with what is actually available? 5. <strong>What must be cut so that the one thing can be completed?</strong></p>\n<h3>The rule</h3>\n<p>&quot;A wise man feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool rageth, and is confident.&quot; (Proverbs 14:16, KJV). A costed vision is more spiritual than an unpaid one.</p>"},{"slug":"05-MERCY-AND-MARKET","title":"05 — MERCY AND MARKET","html":"<h2>05 — MERCY AND MARKET</h2>\n<h4>The customer is a neighbour</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;Let all your things be done with charity.&quot; (1 Corinthians 16:14, KJV) &quot;Whether therefore ye eat, or drink, or whatsoever ye do, do all to the glory of God.&quot; (1 Corinthians 10:31, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p>A project of choice can easily become a project of self. These tests keep the Heart and Mind governing the Hand.</p>\n<h3>The three tests before any pricing, sale or launch</h3>\n<p>1. <strong>Who is served?</strong> Name the actual person, not a demographic. If you cannot name them, you do not yet know your work. 2. <strong>Who is excluded?</strong> Is anyone priced out who should not be? What will you do for them anyway? 3. <strong>Who is harmed?</strong> Does the work cost a family time, rest or dignity that it should not?</p>\n<h3>The four rules</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Practice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Price honestly</td><td>No false scarcity, no invented urgency, no manufactured testimonials</td></tr><tr><td>Serve the poor deliberately</td><td>Decide in advance what portion of the work is done freely — and record it</td></tr><tr><td>Keep rest sacred</td><td>No Sunday trading that destroys the household&#x27;s worship and rest</td></tr><tr><td>Tell the truth about results</td><td>No invented income figures, no exaggerated claims, no &quot;blessing&quot; language to hide a bad decision</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The weekly mercy line</h3>\n<p>Every week, your project must include <strong>one act that cannot be justified by profit</strong>. Record it in the Book of the Righteous: &quot;The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.&quot; (Psalm 37:21, KJV).</p>\n<h3>If the project grows</h3>\n<p>Growth is not a verdict on your faithfulness. &quot;And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work&quot; (2 Corinthians 9:8, KJV). Sufficiency is for abounding, not accumulating. If growth costs you the household, it is not the work.</p>\n<h3>Warning</h3>\n<p>This is not a promise of income, and it is not a prosperity teaching. The measure of the year is not revenue. It is a whole person — hand, heart and mind — in a whole household, doing one faithful work.</p>"},{"slug":"06-DISCERNMENT-REGISTER","title":"06 — DISCERNMENT REGISTER","html":"<h2>06 — DISCERNMENT REGISTER</h2>\n<h4>One thing to stop, one to start, one to keep</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.&quot; (James 1:5, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p>Opened at Week 36 and updated monthly to the end of the year.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>STOP (what I will no longer do)</th><th>START (what I will now do)</th><th>KEEP (what I will not let go)</th><th>Verse / reason</th><th>Date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>September</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>October</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>November</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>December</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Extra corrections</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>What was corrected</th><th>Evidence that it changed</th><th>Who checked it</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>\n<h3>The rule of the register</h3>\n<p>A vision that survives a year unchanged has probably not been reviewed. &quot;But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.&quot; (James 1:25, KJV).</p>"},{"slug":"07-QUARTERLY-PROJECT-REVIEW","title":"07 — QUARTERLY PROJECT REVIEW","html":"<h2>07 — QUARTERLY PROJECT REVIEW</h2>\n<h4>Four reviews; four chances to re-scope rather than quit</h4>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Review</th><th>Week</th><th>Question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Q1</td><td>17</td><td>Is the one project real?</td></tr><tr><td>Q2 / Second Wind</td><td>26</td><td>Is it still the right size for the second half?</td></tr><tr><td>Q3</td><td>39</td><td>Is it being proved in action?</td></tr><tr><td>Q4</td><td>48</td><td>What will be carried into 2028?</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Review template (copy per quarter)</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Quarter / dates</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The single project</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What actually exists now (evidence)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Deliverables completed</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Deliverables not completed</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What the Cost Sheet now says</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>What the family says (honestly)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mercy acts recorded</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Discernment corrections made</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Decision</strong> — continue / re-scope / pause / close</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>If re-scoped, the new one-page statement</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>New deadline</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Member signature</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The re-scope rule</h3>\n<p>A project may be <strong>re-scoped, not replaced</strong>, except at Q2 where a project may be closed and a smaller one chosen. Always write the change; never swap silently. &quot;And I will take of the spirit which is upon thee, and will put it upon them; and they shall bear the burden of the people with thee, that thou bear it not thyself alone.&quot; (Numbers 11:17, KJV).</p>\n<h3>Closing a project</h3>\n<p>Closing is not failure. A closed project that taught the household what it could not carry has produced real evidence. Record what it taught in the Book of the Mind and move on without shame.</p>"},{"slug":"08-FIRE-PROTOCOL-CARDS","title":"08 — FIRE PROTOCOL CARDS","html":"<h2>08 — FIRE PROTOCOL CARDS</h2>\n<h4>Keep these on your phone</h4>\n<p><strong>Governing verse:</strong> &quot;The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.&quot; (Leviticus 6:13, KJV)</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Say this</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Monday declaration</td><td>&quot;One sentence is enough — what will exist by Friday?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Wednesday spark</td><td>&quot;It is Wednesday. What exists right now that did not exist on Monday?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Friday evidence</td><td>&quot;Post DONE, PARTIAL or NOT DONE with a link, a name or a date. All three are acceptable; silence is not.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>First silence</td><td>&quot;I haven&#x27;t seen your declaration. I&#x27;m not assuming anything.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>No Wednesday reply</td><td>&quot;Checking in. What exists now?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>No evidence by 20:00</td><td>&quot;I&#x27;m calling because I didn&#x27;t see evidence. No lecture — what got in the way?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Seven days silent</td><td>&quot;You&#x27;ve been quiet for seven days. I&#x27;m pairing you with someone for a week — not as a correction, but because &#x27;two are better than one.&#x27;&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Fourteen days silent</td><td>&quot;I want to reset with you, not reprimand you. What did you intend? What happened? What is the smallest faithful next step?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Lost heart</td><td>&quot;You have not failed. You have been carrying a plan too heavy. Let&#x27;s find the smaller thing you can finish this week.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>First Re-fire</td><td>&quot;Re-read Week 1. Write a smaller seven-day deliverable. Pair with someone still moving.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Second Wind</td><td>&quot;Most January resolutions are already dead. Re-count the cost. Discard one thing. Re-declare one smaller thing.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Public monthly read</td><td>&quot;We read the record as evidence, not as verdict. Where there is a gap, we name it plainly and move on.&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Never say</h3>\n<ul><li>&quot;You always do this.&quot;</li><li>&quot;If you really had faith you would…&quot;</li><li>&quot;The whole group is waiting on you.&quot;</li><li>&quot;At least you tried.&quot; (It closes the conversation.)</li><li>Anything that turns the record into a weapon.</li></ul>\n<h3>Remember</h3>\n<p>&quot;For it is God which worketh in you both to will and to do of his good pleasure.&quot; (Philippians 2:13, KJV). You stir the fire; you are not the fire&#x27;s source.</p>"},{"slug":"09-PROTECTIONS","title":"09 — PROTECTIONS","html":"<h2>09 — PROTECTIONS</h2>\n<h4>Read before you begin</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.&quot; (Romans 12:1, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p>The ground of every imperative in this year is <strong>mercy</strong>, not threat. These protections are binding.</p>\n<p>1. <strong>Not a prosperity teaching.</strong> No promise of income is made. Revenue is not a measure of faithfulness, and no one is to imply that it is. 2. <strong>Not a verdict.</strong> The record is evidence, not a judgment on a person. &quot;if our heart condemn us, God is greater than our heart&quot; (1 John 3:20, KJV). 3. <strong>Family before project.</strong> A project that costs a household its peace, worship or rest is re-scoped or closed. &quot;And let them make me a sanctuary; that I may dwell among them&quot; (Exodus 25:8, KJV). 4. <strong>One project only.</strong> Ambition that multiplies projects is usually avoidance in disguise. Finish one thing. 5. <strong>No fabricated numbers.</strong> No invented income figures, testimonials, statistics or results. &quot;Let him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his hands the thing which is good&quot; (Ephesians 4:28, KJV). 6. <strong>No moralising of tiredness.</strong> Depression, anxiety and exhaustion are burdens to carry, not sins to rebuke. Rest is commanded. 7. <strong>Confidentiality before visibility.</strong> The Book of the Heart never exposes a recipient. Names may be withheld on request. 8. <strong>Accountability is not condemnation.</strong> If a person fears the record, they will lie to it. A lying record is worse than an empty one. 9. <strong>The fire needs a fire.</strong> The person serving as accountability fire must have someone who checks them. &quot;Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.&quot; (Proverbs 27:17, KJV).</p>\n<hr>\n<p><em>Where this pack disagrees with <code>PILLAR-SCHEMA.md</code>, the schema wins; where both disagree with Scripture, Scripture wins — in KJV, unaltered.</em></p>"},{"slug":"10-SELF-RULE-OF-LIFE","title":"10 — SELF RULE OF LIFE","html":"<h2>10 — SELF RULE OF LIFE</h2>\n<h4>The root field: hand, heart and mind</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p>Everything else grows from this field. If the self is divided, the family, the business and the nation work will all be double-minded — &quot;cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded&quot; (James 4:8, KJV).</p>\n<h3>The three-minute daily presentation</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Faculty</th><th>Words</th><th>One question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Hand</strong></td><td>&quot;Lord, these hands today — your work.&quot;</td><td>What will I make or do that serves someone?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Heart</strong></td><td>&quot;This heart today — your love.&quot;</td><td>Whom do I need to love well today?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mind</strong></td><td>&quot;This mind today — your truth.&quot;</td><td>What do I believe that I have not examined?</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Daily practices</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>KJV anchor</th><th>What it actually is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Truth</td><td>&quot;thy word have I hid in mine heart&quot; (Psalm 119:11)</td><td>One verse kept in mind through the day</td></tr><tr><td>Attention</td><td>&quot;think on these things&quot; (Philippians 4:8)</td><td>One true thing to dwell on when the mind wanders</td></tr><tr><td>Confession</td><td>&quot;Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another&quot; (James 5:16)</td><td>One named failure, told to one trusted person</td></tr><tr><td>Rest</td><td>&quot;Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while&quot; (Mark 6:31)</td><td>An unprogrammed day, kept</td></tr><tr><td>Body</td><td>&quot;glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God&#x27;s&quot; (1 Corinthians 6:20)</td><td>Sleep, food, movement treated as stewardship</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Weekly self-examination (Friday)</h3>\n<p>1. Where did my hands work as to the Lord this week? 2. Where did my heart run where I did not want it to? 3. What did I tell myself this week that I would not say in prayer?</p>\n<h3>What this is not</h3>\n<p>Not self-optimisation, not a productivity system, not a mood. &quot;For it is God which worketh in you both to will and to do of his good pleasure&quot; (Philippians 2:13, KJV). The discipline is a response to grace, not a way of earning it.</p>"},{"slug":"11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY","title":"11 — NATION-BUILDING ACTIVITY SHEET","html":"<h2>11 — NATION-BUILDING ACTIVITY SHEET</h2>\n<h4>The horizon field: my country, my part</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;And I will take of the spirit which is upon thee, and will put it upon them; and they shall bear the burden of the people with thee&quot; (Numbers 11:17, KJV). &quot;To do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?&quot; (Micah 6:8, KJV).</blockquote>\n<p>Nation-building here is not politics and not ideology. It is the sum of ordinary, honest, useful acts by which a person strengthens the place God has put them. <strong>Personal</strong> nation-building: what I can do with the hand, heart and mind I actually have.</p>\n<h3>The five forms of personal nation-building</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>What it looks like</th><th>This year&#x27;s smallest version</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Honest work</strong></td><td>Doing your business or job with skill and integrity — no false weights, no shortcuts</td><td>One standard you will not lower</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Order</strong></td><td>Keeping a street, a neighbourhood, a group or an online space usable and clean</td><td>One place you will improve monthly</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mercy to the vulnerable</strong></td><td>Feeding, visiting, employing, training or protecting someone who cannot repay</td><td>One named person or household</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Truth and civility</strong></td><td>Refusing corruption, gossip and false witness in public and online speech</td><td>One thing you will not repeat or sign</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Building capacity</strong></td><td>Teaching a skill, mentoring one person, creating one useful thing that outlasts you</td><td>One person you will train</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>My 2027 nation-building commitment</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>My answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One place I will serve</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One person I will train or mentor</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One public/online habit I will refuse</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One honest standard in my work</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>One monthly act of order (clean, repair, organise)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>How my business serves the nation, not only me</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Monthly evidence I will record</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The integrity test</h3>\n<p>Before any public act, message or transaction:</p>\n<p>1. Would I say this in the online gathering with my family present? 2. Does it make the weaker person better off, or only me? 3. Can it be recorded without shame?</p>\n<blockquote>&quot;He that walketh with wise men shall be wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed.&quot; (Proverbs 13:20, KJV)</blockquote>\n<h3>Protection</h3>\n<p>Nation-building is not a platform for self-importance, partisan bitterness or saving the country by yourself. &quot;Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it&quot; (Psalm 127:1, KJV). Do the small faithful thing; leave the rest to God.</p>"},{"slug":"12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER","title":"12 — FOUR FIELDS PLANNER","html":"<h2>12 — FOUR FIELDS PLANNER</h2>\n<h4>One page per week</h4>\n<p><strong>Week ___</strong> · Dates ____________ · Member ____________</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>This week&#x27;s one deliverable</th><th>Who it serves</th><th>Evidence due Friday</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong> (the one project)</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Wednesday spark (one question per field)</h3>\n<ul><li>Self: what did you examine this week?</li><li>Family: what did you do together?</li><li>Business: what exists now that did not exist on Monday?</li><li>Nation: what did you strengthen?</li></ul>\n<h3>Friday evidence</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>DONE / PARTIAL / NOT DONE</th><th>The proof</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Family</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Business</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Nation</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The one rule</h3>\n<p>Four fields, <strong>four small deliverables</strong>, not four large projects. The business is the only one allowed to grow into an enterprise this year. The others grow by faithfulness, not by scale.</p>\n<blockquote>&quot;Inspired to Create. Anchored in Love. Guided by Wisdom. All to the glory of God.&quot;</blockquote>"},{"slug":"13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK","title":"13 — FIVE-DIMENSIONS CHECK","html":"<h2>13 — FIVE-DIMENSIONS CHECK</h2>\n<h4>Every session, every week, every person</h4>\n<blockquote>&quot;And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.&quot; (1 Thessalonians 5:23, KJV)</blockquote>\n<p>This is a <strong>diagnostic</strong>, not a new authority. It is a way of asking whether the biblical work of hand, heart and mind has reached the whole person. Scripture governs the framework; the framework never governs Scripture.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What it means here</th><th>KJV anchor</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Spiritual</strong></td><td>Consecration, prayer, Scripture, worship — the heart before God</td><td>&quot;Create in me a clean heart, O God&quot; (Psalm 51:10)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mental</strong></td><td>Belief, discernment, review, the discipline of attention</td><td>&quot;be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind&quot; (Romans 12:2)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>The body: work, rest, food, sleep, movement, the actual making</td><td>&quot;present your bodies a living sacrifice&quot; (Romans 12:1)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Social</strong></td><td>Household, friendship, community, citizenship — love in deed</td><td>&quot;love thy neighbour as thyself&quot; (Mark 12:31)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Financial</strong></td><td>Money, cost, work, giving, stewardship — the business field</td><td>&quot;counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it&quot; (Luke 14:28)</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The Friday check — rate each 1–5 and write one line</h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>1–5</th><th>Evidence from this week</th><th>One correction for next week</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spiritual</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Mental</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Physical</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Social</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>The diagnostic questions</h3>\n<p>1. <strong>Spiritual:</strong> Did I pray, read and obey — or only feel? 2. <strong>Mental:</strong> What did I learn that changed a decision? 3. <strong>Physical:</strong> Did I use my hands and keep my rest? 4. <strong>Social:</strong> Whom did I love in deed, not only in word? 5. <strong>Financial:</strong> Did I count the cost and tell the truth about money?</p>\n<h3>The rule</h3>\n<p>A weak dimension is not a sin to confess in public. It is a field to tend. &quot;And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not&quot; (Galatians 6:9, KJV).</p>\n<hr>"},{"slug":"README","title":"2027 RESOURCE PACK","html":"<h2>2027 RESOURCE PACK</h2>\n<h3>Family · one project · accountability fire</h3>\n<p>These are working tools, not more teaching. Copy them into your shared drive, print them if you want, and fill them in. <strong>A resource that is not filled in is not a resource.</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Resource</th><th>Use it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01</td><td>[Project Charter](01-PROJECT-CHARTER.md)</td><td>Choose and define the <strong>one</strong> project. Fill in Week 3–4.</td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>[Family Rule of Life](02-FAMILY-RULE-OF-LIFE.md)</td><td>The daily and weekly household rhythm. Fill in Week 1.</td></tr><tr><td>03</td><td>[Weekly Accountability Sheet](03-WEEKLY-ACCOUNTABILITY-SHEET.md)</td><td>Declare / Spark / Evidence. Every week.</td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>[Cost Sheet](04-COST-SHEET.md)</td><td>Real numbers against the project. Week 13 and again at Second Wind.</td></tr><tr><td>05</td><td>[Mercy and Market](05-MERCY-AND-MARKET.md)</td><td>Keep the project in love. Use at pricing and customer decisions.</td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>[Discernment Register](06-DISCERNMENT-REGISTER.md)</td><td>Stop / start / keep. Monthly from Week 36.</td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>[Quarterly Project Review](07-QUARTERLY-PROJECT-REVIEW.md)</td><td>Q1–Q4 reviews. Weeks 17, 26, 39, 48.</td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>[Fire Protocol Cards](08-FIRE-PROTOCOL-CARDS.md)</td><td>Scripts for the accountability fire. Keep on your phone.</td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>[Protections](09-PROTECTIONS.md)</td><td>What this is not. Read before you begin.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>[Self Rule of Life](10-SELF-RULE-OF-LIFE.md)</td><td>Hand, Heart, Mind — the root field.</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>[Nation-Building Activity Sheet](11-NATION-BUILDING-ACTIVITY.md)</td><td>The horizon field — citizenship, service, integrity, nation-building.</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>[Four Fields Planner](12-FOUR-FIELDS-PLANNER.md)</td><td>One page a week covering Self, Family, Business and Nation.</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>[Five-Dimensions Check](13-FIVE-DIMENSIONS-CHECK.md)</td><td>Spiritual · Mental · Physical · Social · Financial — every session, every week.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><strong>The four fields of work in 2027:</strong></p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Scope</th><th>Governing question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Self</strong></td><td>Hand, Heart, Mind — my own consecration</td><td>Am I whole before God?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Family</strong></td><td>My household — the first human work</td><td>Does my house become more whole through this year?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business</strong></td><td>One focused project of my choice</td><td>Does one real thing exist that serves real people?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nation</strong></td><td>My personal nation-building activity</td><td>Does my work strengthen the country God has placed me in?</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>These are not four projects. They are <strong>four dimensions of one life</strong>. The business is the economic engine; the family is the first field; the self is the root; the nation is the horizon.</p>\n<p><strong>The rule of one:</strong> one household, one business project, one deliverable each week, one piece of evidence each Friday. A second business may not begin until the first has been reviewed at a quarterly review or the Second Wind.</p>\n<p>Scripture is KJV throughout. Governing documents: <code>2027CLW/PILLAR-SCHEMA.md</code>, <code>2027CLW/THE-ACCOUNTABILITY-FIRE.md</code>, <code>2027CLW/2027-WEEKLY-CURRICULUM.md</code>.</p>"}]};
